# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# Enable dropped while moving (LinuxCNC's machine off or estop, the link
# still up): en_stop = 1 runs the quick stop, then the outputs go off, with
# no fault. en_stop = 0 coasts, as before. No link timeout to wait for, so
# shorter than estop_link.test (~1.2 rad).
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
lcnc 0 300
run 0.004
fault0.stop
run 0.3
hv0.sim_dist
hv0.sim_vel
fault0.fault
fault0.state
fault0.en_out
@expect fault0.stop[1] == 1
@expect hv0.sim_dist ~ 1.2 0.4
@expect hv0.sim_vel[2] ~ 0 0.5
@expect fault0.fault == 0
@expect fault0.state == 0
@expect fault0.en_out == 0
